      "rationale": "A binary presence flag is useful for distinguishing quantified financial goals but is coarse. Some readings look generous: a customer satisfaction 78%->90% goal marked True for financial quantification is questionable, since the percentages are non-financial, slightly undermining groundedness."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
  "source_groundedness": 0.83,
  "rationale": "The added columns supply several genuine, query-relevant axes (metric alignment, mechanism, scope, horizon) that let an analyst group and model goal achievement, going well beyond the original fields. Values are mostly sound readings of the description/metric/category text. Minor groundedness concerns include a broad 'financial_quantification_present' flag firing on non-financial percentage targets and an occasional horizon overreach ('upcoming year'->multi_year), but no systematic invention of facts. goal_outcome_type is somewhat redundant with the existing category column, capping its usefulness."
